From 079f97d50f7b11686cb518af150172f49d37bed7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LightMoss <noreply@github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:18:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: rpminiv2: report touch in the landscape
 frame

The Mini V2's 1080x1240 panel is mounted right side up (rotation = <90>,
the connector's "panel orientation" is "Right Side Up"), so its right
edge is at the top of the casing and the picture everything draws is
1240x1080 landscape. The FocalTech touchscreen still reports the
panel's portrait frame. DRM leaves it to userspace to turn touch with
the picture, which ROCKNIX does in sway (map_to_output), but LightMoss
has no compositor: SDL2/SDL3 programs, RetroArch's udev pointer and
the emulators read the evdev node directly and got every touch turned
90 degrees.

Turn it here, once, for every reader: touchscreen-inverted-x and
touchscreen-swapped-x-y make the driver report X = panel y (0..1239)
and Y = 1079 - panel x (0..1079), the inverse of the 90 degree
clockwise turn that puts the landscape picture on the panel. A touch at
the panel's top-left corner (0,0), which is the bottom-left of the
landscape picture, now reads (0,1079); the panel's top-right corner
(1079,0) is the picture's top-left and reads (0,0). ROCKNIX's AYN Thor
Lite bottom screen, the same CH13726A 1080x1240 panel with
rotation = <90>, uses the same two properties.
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-retroidpocket-rpminiv2.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-retroidpocket-rpminiv2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-retroidpocket-rpminiv2.dts
index e5f4ac022..3263ef932 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-retroidpocket-rpminiv2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-retroidpocket-rpminiv2.dts
@@ -16,6 +16,14 @@ &i2c13 {
 	touchscreen@38 {
 		touchscreen-size-x = <1080>;
 		touchscreen-size-y = <1240>;
+		/*
+		 * The panel is mounted right side up (rotation = <90>) and
+		 * nothing above the kernel turns touch with the picture, so
+		 * report the upright landscape frame: X = panel y (0..1239),
+		 * Y = 1079 - panel x (0..1079).
+		 */
+		touchscreen-inverted-x;
+		touchscreen-swapped-x-y;
 	};
 };
 
